SolarBench derived data — licence and attribution
==================================================

This file covers the DERIVED data products in this repository. Source code is
covered separately by LICENSE (Apache-2.0).


1. What this licence covers
---------------------------

Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) applies to the
derived protocol and result files produced by this project:

    protocol/splits_*.csv          site-to-split assignment and date boundaries
    protocol/capacity_*.csv        per-site capacity normalization constants
    protocol/rare_events_*.csv     rare-event label counts per site and split
    protocol/protocol_summary.csv  per-dataset summary
    results/*.csv                  baseline results for every model and seed

Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Attribution requirement. If you use these files, cite the paper (see
CITATION.cff) and state that the protocol definitions come from SolarBench.


2. What this licence does NOT cover
-----------------------------------

SolarBench does not redistribute any source dataset. No raw measurement, and
no harmonized copy of a raw measurement, is included in this repository. The
files above contain only derived quantities: split labels, aggregate counts,
percentile constants and model error metrics.

The CC BY 4.0 grant is made only to the extent this project holds rights in
these derived products. It does not, and cannot, grant rights in the
underlying source data. Each source dataset remains under the terms of its
original provider, and you must obtain each one yourself.


